  1:Name            D4-SADOD Bus enable to address converter and cycle end logic;
  2:PartNo          108393-001;
  3:Revision        01;
  4:Date            16/5/26;
  5:Designer        Dave Henry;
  6:Company         Breadboarding Labs;
  7:Location        None;
  8:Assembly        None;
  9:Device          p22v10;
 10:
 11:/* 16/05/2026 V1 Initial version converted from PALASM format in COMPAQ design doc         */
 12:/*                                                                                         */
 13:/*******************************************************************************************/
 14:/*                                                                                         */
 15:/*******************************************************************************************/
 16:/*
 17:DESCRIPTION
 18:This PAL converts the CPUs bus enable lines to address lines and cycles from 
 19:one to the next when multiple cycles are required. It also determines_when 
 20:the last cycle is in progress to develop the Cycle LAST signal. 
 21:Rev A of this device changes the CX16* equation to go away on ALE. The input 
 22:T01 is changed to T10 and IO16* is changed to LM_IO as part of an overall 
 23:change to delay the sampling of IO16* by one clock. Rev A can be used in any 
 24:D4-PROCESSOR from rev X5 up.
 25:Rev D is for the D4-Processor Enhanced (397 version)
 26:
 27:*/
 28:
 29:/* Pin Map 
 30:                               ______________
 31:                              |   D4-SADOD   |
 32:                     CALE x---|1           24|---x Vcc                      
 33:                      ALE x---|2           23|---x !RST                     
 34:                     !BE3 x---|3           22|---x !DCMD                    
 35:                     !BE2 x---|4           21|---x !CX16                    
 36:                     !BE1 x---|5           20|---x !ALST                    
 37:                     !BE0 x---|6           19|---x !BHE                     
 38:                    LM_IO x---|7           18|---x A0                       
 39:                      T00 x---|8           17|---x A1                       
 40:                      T10 x---|9           16|---x !CLSTD                   
 41:                    !LM16 x---|10          15|---x !CLAST                   
 42:                    !IO16 x---|11          14|---x !CMD                     
 43:                      GND x---|12          13|---x BHLDA                    
 44:                              |______________|
 45:
 46:*/
 47:
 48:/*******************************************************************************************/
 49:
 50:/* Inputs Note GAL20V10 Pin 23 and 14 are also inputs. Only Pins 15-22 can be Outputs */
 51:
 52:
